<title>GERMANY: BSHG submits bid for Amana of U.S.</title>
<headline>BSHG submits bid for Amana of U.S.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bosch Siemens Hausgeraete GmbH said on Tuesday it had submitted a bid for U.S. household appliance maker Amana, a unit of Raytheon.</p>
<p>&quot;We have started the bidding process,&quot; BSHG chief executive Herbert Woerner told the company's annual results news conference.</p>
<p>Woerner said there were many bidders, however, and he did not know if his company's bid would succeed.</p>
<p>Amana, with 8,000 employees, has sales of about $1.5 billion.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
